  <content>
  <section>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="a0fd30b4-1e67-45b1-8b6d-333169c6fea6" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.
  </para>
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="47aa30b9-ab56-418a-b39c-4ec8704c046e" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(2+2+2+2+2+2+2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2 \\cdot 7\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2+7\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which expression equals \(2^7\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d4ae43a2-6c9d-4eb8-9bea-7160d3e0bea9" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="exponential function" data-solution-options="[&quot;linear function&quot;, &quot;exponential function&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The graph shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account A. The table shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account B.

          <para><figure><media alt="Graph of a function on grid."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f84cb93fa8c368dc50ad53c8747843ba76f3d08f"/></media></figure></para>
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Number of years</entry>
                <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Amount in dollars</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  0
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,000
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  1
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,150
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  2
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,300
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  3
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,450
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  4
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,600
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          
        </para>
      <para>Investment A is a/n:</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.3.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2e8018d8-02b2-44d7-93ec-2d588f989d63" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="linear function" data-solution-options="[&quot;linear function&quot;, &quot;exponential function&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Investment B is a/n:</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="fbad6471-c6ee-45b1-bc1d-256b4c9d53e3" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;Investment A has a common ratio.&quot;, &quot;Investment B is growing by the same number of dollars each year.&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;Investment A has a higher initial balance than investment B.&quot;, &quot;Investment A has a common ratio.&quot;, &quot;Investment B has a common ratio.&quot;, &quot;Investment A is growing by the same number of dollars each year.&quot;, &quot;Investment B is growing by the same number of dollars each year.&quot;, &quot;After 12 years, investment B will result in more money.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The graph shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account A. The table shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account B.

          <para><figure><media alt="Graph of a function on grid."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f84cb93fa8c368dc50ad53c8747843ba76f3d08f"/></media></figure></para>
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Number of years</entry>
                <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Amount in dollars</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  0
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,000
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  1
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,150
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  2
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,300
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  3
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,450
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  4
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  $2,600
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          
        </para>
      <para>Which of the following statements are true? <emphasis>Select two</emphasis> that apply.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q4a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5194cfd4-7a35-4cf5-8e07-a1591abd5323" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="1" data-solution-options="[&quot;1&quot;, &quot;5&quot;, &quot;10&quot;, &quot;15&quot;]">
    <problem>

      <para>Investment account 1 starts with a balance of $200 and doubles every year. Investment account 2 starts with $1,000 and increases by $100 each year.  How long does it take for each account to double?</para>
      <para>How many years will it take investment account 1 to double?</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.1.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q4b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="612a528e-7954-4e6c-9072-ab22608e43cc" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="10" data-solution-options="[&quot;1&quot;, &quot;5&quot;, &quot;10&quot;, &quot;15&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>How many years will it take investment account 2 to double?</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.1.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6b5c04b5-8090-4f89-a000-25b2f7d21a5a" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="30,000" data-solution-options="[&quot;10,003&quot;, &quot;10,300&quot;, &quot;30,000&quot;, &quot;90,000&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>A population of ants is 10,000 at the start of April. Since then, it triples each month. How many ants will there be 1 month later? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.3.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b2a066e0-6c5c-444e-bed3-c0ebd63e6c9a" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="90,000, 270,000, 510,000" data-solution-options="[&quot;50,000, 70,000, 90,000&quot;, &quot;90,000, 270,000, 510,000&quot;, &quot;40,000, 70,000, 110,000&quot;, &quot;33,000, 33,300, 33,330&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>A population of ants is 10,000 at the start of April. Since then, it triples each month. Which values complete the table?
          
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">months since April</entry>
                <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">number of ants</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  0
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  10,000
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  1
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  30,000
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  2
                </entry>
                <entry>
                   
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  3
                </entry>
                <entry>
                   
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  4
                </entry>
                <entry>
                   
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7fc355fd-7699-488f-8921-1f1e256f30ac" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(3n\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\( 3^n\\)&quot;, &quot;\\( n^3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(3n\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(n+3\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>A population of ants triples each month. If there are \(n\) ants in one month, which expression represents how many ants there will be one month later?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="87c78b8b-26b8-41e3-8460-5a784a34a678" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(500+24 \cdot 8\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(500 \\cdot 24 \\cdot 8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(500+24+8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(500+24 \\cdot 8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(500\\cdot 248\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>A swimming pool contains 500 gallons of water. A hose is turned on, and it fills the pool at a rate of 24 gallons per minute. Which expression represents the amount of water in the pool, in gallons, after 8 minutes?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e92fbc0f-e497-4ac1-a2d8-845e0aa31bd2" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(100,000 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(100,000 \\cdot 2^5\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;32,000&quot;, &quot;320,000&quot;, &quot;\\(100,000 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(100,000 \\cdot 5^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(100,000 \\cdot 2^5\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The population of a city is 100,000. It doubles each decade for 5 decades. <emphasis>Select the two</emphasis> expressions that represent the population of the city after 5 decades. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="bc09b419-b906-4baa-a7fe-96fe89ca2aa1" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Account C will contain more money than account D after 10 weeks." data-solution-options="[&quot;Account C will contain more money than account D after 2 weeks.&quot;, &quot;Account C will never contain more money than account D.&quot;, &quot;Account C will contain more money than account D after 7 weeks.&quot;, &quot;Account C will contain more money than account D after 10 weeks.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Bank account C starts with $10 and doubles each week. Bank account D starts with $1,000 and grows by $500 each week.
          <para>When will account C contain more money than account D? </para>
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.3.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
